## Local preview server

Ting now works through Codex rather than Cursor. Cursor's folder-open auto-start is disabled so it does not secretly start a second preview on port 3000.

**Agents (Codex):**

- Use one local preview only, defaulting to **http://127.0.0.1:3001**.
- Do not run `npm run dev:restart` from Codex as a normal foreground command. It is long-running, and if the command window times out it can leave the preview half-alive.
- Start preview as a hidden background process with its own log file, using `npm.cmd run dev -- --hostname 127.0.0.1 --port 3001`.
- Before starting preview, check whether the chosen port is already listening. If it is healthy, reuse it.
- If preview is stuck, stop only the process listening on the exact preview port. Never `taskkill` or stop all `node` processes.
- Do not run two previews from the same `miozuki-web` folder at the same time; Next dev shares local build state and can wedge.

Debug logs: `.next/dev/logs/next-development.log` and the preview-specific log file created by Codex.

